---
title: Tater Tot Hotdish
description: Beef and mushroom tater tot casserole where a from-scratch Parmesan sauce replaces the canned soup.
tags: [casserole, make-ahead, winter]
course: main
icons: [potato, mushroom, pan-food]
cuisine: American
source:
  name: America's Test Kitchen
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/10044-tater-tot-hotdish
servings: 6
time: 1h45m
---

Adjust an oven rack to the upper-middle position and heat the oven to 450°F (230°C).

Combine the @85 percent lean ground beef{1 1/2%lb}, @white mushrooms{1%lb}(trimmed and sliced thin), @onion{1}(chopped), @garlic cloves{4}(minced), @fresh thyme{1%tbsp}(minced), @salt{1 1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1 1/2%tsp} in a #Dutch oven{}. Cook over medium-high heat until nearly all the liquid has evaporated, ~cook{25-28%minutes}, stirring occasionally and breaking up the meat with a #spoon{}.

Stir in the @all-purpose flour{3%tbsp} until fully incorporated and cook for ~cook{1%minute}.

Stir in the @whole milk{1 1/2%cup} and @chicken broth{1 1/2%cup} and bring to a simmer, scraping up any browned bits. Cook until the mixture is slightly thickened, about ~simmer{3%minutes}.

Off the heat, stir in the @Parmesan cheese{85%g}(3 oz, grated, 1 1/2 cups). Transfer the mixture to a 13-by-9-inch #baking dish{}.

Sprinkle the @frozen peas{1%cup} and @frozen corn{1%cup} evenly over the beef mixture.

Lightly arrange the @frozen tater tots{2%lb}(1 bag) in an even layer over the top, but do not press them into the mixture (you may have extra tater tots).

Bake until the tater tots are deep golden brown and the filling is bubbling, ~bake{35-38%minutes}, rotating the dish halfway through baking. Let cool for ~cool{15%minutes} before serving.

> **Making ahead** — After moving the beef mixture to the baking dish, let it cool completely, then cover with aluminum foil and refrigerate for up to 24 hours. To serve, bake the beef mixture, covered, until hot in the center, 15 to 20 minutes. Remove the foil, stir the beef mixture, sprinkle with the peas and corn, arrange the tater tots on top, and bake as directed.
